              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, section\u202f1447(c) provides for a fee award when a case is remanded to state court, but there is no statute allowing a fee award to a defendant who removes and successfully defends a motion to remand."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "56020f80f97b5d0067ac93ebb4519d0f2367e4eb21cf0a0f17ea2bd1b0bffa90",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-56020f80f97b-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 19,
                "start": 19
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners argue that removal should be limited to cases where the argument is strong enough to justify the cost."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "56020f80f97b5d0067ac93ebb4519d0f2367e4eb21cf0a0f17ea2bd1b0bffa90",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-56020f80f97b-0002-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 46,
                "start": 46
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, according to Mr. Holdman, there was no finding by the district court of any manipulative intent in the removal, nor any suggestion that such intent should deny fees."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Holdman",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "56020f80f97b5d0067ac93ebb4519d0f2367e4eb21cf0a0f17ea2bd1b0bffa90",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-56020f80f97b-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 20,
                "start": 20
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Holdman, mr. Holdman expressed uncertainty whether the Seventh Circuit would limit the presumption to extraordinary circumstances."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner (Martin)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "56020f80f97b5d0067ac93ebb4519d0f2367e4eb21cf0a0f17ea2bd1b0bffa90",
              "evidence_ids": [
